 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 7680,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The first copied byte in the scene record is $03. The caller starts executing one byte later."
  },
  {
   "address": 7681,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Save and reload the caller stack pointer, copy the score digits, set up screen and colour pointers, use sound request $87 and initialize expanded sprite 1 before applying the scene colour lookup."
  },
  {
   "address": 7684,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Restore the saved stack pointer, copy the digit characters and initialize score pointers. Select the room sprite configuration and start sound $87 before switching the VIC bank."
  },
  {
   "address": 7804,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Set sprite 1 to X=$9F and Y=$34. Expand it in both directions, put it behind the background and select its colour 7 before applying the room colour table."
  },
  {
   "address": 10492,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Save the expected action in $10 and read the joystick with active-low bits inverted. Return the expected mask on an exact match. No input returns $FF. An incorrect nonzero mask also requests sound $89 and starts a 20-call cooldown."
  },
  {
   "address": 10785,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Update sprite 2 on expiry of $31A4. Add the two velocity bytes, toggle the high X bit on a low-byte wrap and change its vertical behaviour at the $E0 threshold."
  },
  {
   "address": 10994,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Repeat the timed joystick and sprite updates using the initial count in A. Update the weapon-room animation on each iteration."
  },
  {
   "address": 11011,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Wait through two CIA2 timer intervals, poll the joystick and apply the sprite cycle update. Repeat with the count in A saved to $2EC6."
  },
  {
   "address": 11029,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Every three calls advance $31A2 down through 2, 1, 0 and write pointer $BA plus that index to sprite 1."
  },
  {
   "address": 11060,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Use the shared 90-byte record index at $3200. Wait for the lower raster and copy the record to the zero-page sprite work area."
  },
  {
   "address": 11176,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Use the animation index in A to look up sprite 0 coordinates and expansion bits. Set pointer $A9, enable the sprite and load the neighbouring sprite state from the same indexed family."
  },
  {
   "address": 12757,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "This scene record ends with the eleven byte marker copied by the unpacker at $0DDE."
  },
  {
   "address": 16384,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The first page of the screen matrix for the background in VIC bank $4000. Its character codes index the scene colour lookup when the display is initialized."
  },
  {
   "address": 16640,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Screen matrix offsets $100\u2013$1FF. The VIC reads these as character codes and the palette routine processes a page at a time."
  },
  {
   "address": 16896,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Screen matrix offsets $200\u2013$2FF. The screen maps into the glyph data at $7800."
  },
  {
   "address": 17152,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The last page of the screen matrix, including the hardware sprite pointers at $43F8\u2013$43FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 17408,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The two sprite fragments before the active player pair at $4480."
  },
  {
   "address": 17536,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Two 64-byte sprite images for hardware sprites 5 and 6 at the Weapons Room capture."
  },
  {
   "address": 17664,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Four individual sprite shapes between the active player pair and the colour table."
  },
  {
   "address": 17920,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Table indexed by the room screen cells when the scene patches $167A to $46 and calls the shared colour routine."
  },
  {
   "address": 18176,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen 64-byte rendered fragments including torso, hand and bent-leg graphics."
  },
  {
   "address": 19200,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Animation parts with compact head and foot shapes in the low slots and angled limbs in the high slots."
  },
  {
   "address": 20224,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen mask fragments immediately before the row of compact leaning poses."
  },
  {
   "address": 21248,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Middle mask set for the player animation with varied angles of legs and armour."
  },
  {
   "address": 22272,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Another set of adjacent sprite fragments showing outlines of boots and legs."
  },
  {
   "address": 23296,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sprite parts in the $6C\u2013$7B pointer range, including the separate pair of straight lower legs."
  },
  {
   "address": 24320,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixty-four-byte sprite pieces for mixed arm, head, and body animation frames."
  },
  {
   "address": 25344,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Rendered bank of fragments continuing the player motion set, including pointed foot and knee shapes."
  },
  {
   "address": 26368,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The 16 sprite records around the pointer $A9 selected for sprite 0 in the later room routine."
  },
  {
   "address": 27392,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Upper range of sprite masks before the expanded sprite, including a circular weapon silhouette at pointer $B8."
  },
  {
   "address": 28416,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The 64-byte image record selected by sprite 1 at the Weapons Room capture. Both expansion bits are set during initialization."
  },
  {
   "address": 28480,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Seven 64-byte slots with separate shapes such as a circular disk, star and fragments of weapons. The code writes pointer $C0 to sprite 2."
  },
  {
   "address": 28928,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The unpacked picture stream initializes $7100\u2013$73FF to zero. These bytes are still zero in the play capture."
  },
  {
   "address": 30720,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The scene character glyph store for VIC bank $4000 and character-base bits 3\u20131 of $D018 set to 7. A character occupies eight consecutive bytes."
  },
  {
   "address": 31744,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The top half of this scene set, from character code $80. The eight-byte glyph slots are used for the scene-specific objects and screen details."
